========================================================================
SECTION 4: Rapidity coordinates on the Cayley helix
========================================================================

Map (L_n/2, F_n*sqrt(5)/2) = (cosh-like, sinh-like) part of phi^n.
Rapidity w_n = arctanh(F_n*sqrt(5)/L_n) when |F*s5| < |L|,
           or arccoth(F_n*sqrt(5)/L_n) when |F*s5| > |L|.

Since phi^n = (L_n + F_n*s5)/2 and |psi|^n = |L_n - F_n*s5|/2,
we have: rapidity = (1/2)*ln(phi^n / |psi|^n) = n * ln(phi)/... 

KEY IDENTITY: L_n^2 - 5*F_n^2 = 4*(-1)^n

